{% comment %}
  sections/expert-quote.liquid

  One endorsement, said by a named person, with the products it is about
  scattered around them.

  ## Why it is not `sections/testimonials.liquid`

  Testimonials is a row of customers: several cards, each a different voice,
  each equally weighted, and the design's job is to make a quantity of praise
  legible. This is the opposite shape — a single voice given the whole width,
  with a face under it and a line drawn from the words to the face so the eye
  makes the connection before it reads the name.

  A merchant who wants five reviews should reach for Testimonials. A merchant
  who has one expert, one founder or one practitioner whose word carries the
  section should reach for this.

  ## What this file is, and what it is not

  It is the frame and the two axes. Everything with content in it is a block:

    Quote and expert   `blocks/_expert-quote-lead.liquid`
    Featured picture   `blocks/_expert-quote-feature.liquid`
    Scattered picture  `blocks/_expert-quote-image.liquid`

  The first two are rendered with `content_for 'block'` rather than through
  `content_for 'blocks'`. That makes them editable but undeletable and
  undraggable, which is what they should be: a section called Expert quote with
  the quote dragged into the scatter is a section a merchant can break by
  accident. Same mechanism, same reason, as `sections/testimonials.liquid`'s
  header and intro panel.

  The scattered pictures are ordinary repeatable blocks, so the drawing's two
  are a starting point rather than a limit.

  ## The shell is `sections/featured-offer.liquid`'s, setting id for setting id

  Container, colour scheme, background media, the four border widths, the two
  radii, the gaps behind a Desktop/Mobile switch, the margins, the stack layer
  and the whole spacing group — every id here is one that section already
  carries, and both reach them through `snippets/spacing.liquid`,
  `snippets/background-media.liquid` and `snippets/container.liquid` rather than
  reimplementing any of it. A merchant who has arranged a Featured offer has
  arranged this one.

  ## The stage is a flex row and the scatter is `order`, not `position`

  The drawing has two photographs floating either side of the centre column,
  staggered so neither lines up with the other. The obvious way to build that is
  `position: absolute` and two pairs of coordinates, and it is the wrong way:
  absolutely positioned children are out of flow, so the section is only as tall
  as its centre column and a merchant who picks a taller photograph gets one
  hanging out of the bottom of the section and over whatever follows it.

  So the stage is an ordinary flex row — a picture before the featured one, the
  featured one, a picture after it — and which side a picture lands on is
  `order` rather than source position. Source order stays the order a screen
  reader announces and the Tab key follows: the quote, then the person, then the
  pictures. The stagger is `margin-block-start` on each picture, which is in
  flow, so the row grows to hold whatever the merchant offsets — and a negative
  one lifts a picture up beside the expert, which is the arrangement the drawing
  has.

  ## One rhythm, many styles

  The pictures keep moving after they arrive, and the settings for that are
  split deliberately. **How far** and **how fast** are here, so every picture in
  the section moves to one rhythm and a merchant tunes the whole composition
  from one place. **Which way** — float, sway, zoom, orbit — and **how far into
  the cycle** are on each picture, because pictures rising and falling in unison
  is a lift rather than a drift.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    The background is the colour scheme's until the merchant says otherwise:
    either a colour — or, as the preset ships it, the soft horizontal wash the
    section was drawn on — or a picture behind the whole section.

    Emitted as a real `background` declaration rather than a custom property
    because `color-scheme-container` paints a background *and* a gradient image,
    and only the shorthand clears both.
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    One width per side rather than one for the box, summed into `border_any` so
    the three properties are emitted only when at least one side is drawn — a
    zero-width border with a colour on it is three declarations that paint
    nothing.

    Opacity goes into the colour rather than onto the element: `opacity` on the
    section would fade the quote along with its frame. With no colour picked the
    border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters cannot take an alpha
    channel from, so `color-mix` does the same fade in the browser instead and
    both paths honour the slider.

    Identical to `sections/featured-offer.liquid` and `sections/main-faq.liquid`
    by construction, not by coincidence — same ids, same resolution, same
    stylesheet shape.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'

  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- corners ----

    Four corners, twice — one set per device, behind the same Desktop/Mobile
    switch the padding and the gaps already use.

    The top pair ships at 40 and the bottom pair at 0, because a section is a
    band that lifts away from what is above it and sits flush on what is below:
    a rounded bottom edge leaves two slivers of the page showing through under
    it. They are four sliders rather than one number and a rule, so a merchant
    who wants a fully rounded card can still have one.

    They reach CSS as a single border-radius shorthand, in the order that
    property takes — top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left. Nothing in
    the stylesheet reads them as a bare number, which is what makes sending a
    shorthand safe.

    A phone gets its own four because the same number does not read the same at
    both widths: 40px is a soft lift across 1400px and a heavy scoop out of a
    390px screen. Each mobile corner falls back to its desktop value when the
    setting is missing entirely, so a section saved before these existed keeps
    one shape at every width.
  endcomment
  assign r_tl = s.border_radius_top_left | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign r_tr = s.border_radius_top_right | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign r_bl = s.border_radius_bottom_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign r_br = s.border_radius_bottom_right | default: 0 | plus: 0

  assign r_tl_m = s.border_radius_top_left_mobile | default: r_tl | plus: 0
  assign r_tr_m = s.border_radius_top_right_mobile | default: r_tr | plus: 0
  assign r_bl_m = s.border_radius_bottom_left_mobile | default: r_bl | plus: 0
  assign r_br_m = s.border_radius_bottom_right_mobile | default: r_br | plus: 0
  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the gaps ----

    A Desktop/Mobile pair behind one switch, the shape every other section in
    the theme uses. Both pairs are published unconditionally and
    `assets/base.css` picks which applies at a given width, because the pair the
    merchant is not looking at in the editor is still the pair the other
    breakpoint renders.

    `plus: 0` rather than `default` alone, which would replace a deliberate 0 —
    a gap a merchant can legitimately want when a scattered picture is meant to
    sit flush against the featured one. Each mobile axis falls back to its
    desktop value when the setting is absent entirely, so a section saved before
    the mobile pair existed renders as it did; one added since gets the schema
    default, which is half the desktop one.
  endcomment
  assign gap_x = s.gap_horizontal | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign gap_y = s.gap_vertical | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign gap_x_mobile = s.gap_horizontal_mobile | default: gap_x | plus: 0
  assign gap_y_mobile = s.gap_vertical_mobile | default: gap_y | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the shared rhythm ----

    How far a picture travels and how long it takes, inherited by every picture
    block in the section as custom properties. The style and the phase are each
    picture's own — see the note at the top on why the split falls there.

    Published unconditionally: a picture whose style is None carries no
    animation at all, so there is no state where these reach something that was
    not asking for them.
  endcomment
  assign motion_distance = s.motion_distance | default: 18 | plus: 0
  assign motion_duration = s.motion_duration | default: 4000 | plus: 0

  comment
    One slider, four styles — so the distance has to reach the keyframes as
    three different types: a length for Float and Orbit, an angle for Sway, a
    plain multiplier for Zoom.

    Converted here rather than in the stylesheet, and that is not a preference.
    A rotation cannot be derived from a length in CSS without dividing one
    length by another to strip the unit, and `calc(0deg - 18px * 0.12)` is
    simply invalid — mixing the two types makes the whole expression invalid at
    computed-value time, so `rotate` fell back to `none` and Sway did nothing at
    all. The unit-stripping form that does work, `calc(var(--d) / 1px * 1deg)`,
    is CSS Values 4 division and not a thing to rely on across every browser the
    theme supports.

    The ratios are chosen so the four styles read as about the same amount of
    movement at a given setting: at 18px a picture travels 18px, tips 4.5°, or
    grows 9%.
  endcomment
  assign motion_angle = motion_distance | times: 25 | divided_by: 100.0
  assign motion_scale = motion_distance | times: 5 | divided_by: 1000.0 | plus: 1

  assign stage_classes = 'expert-quote__stage'
  unless s.scatter_on_mobile
    assign stage_classes = stage_classes | append: ' expert-quote__stage--no-scatter-mobile'
  endunless
-%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --expert-quote-radius: {{ r_tl }}px {{ r_tr }}px {{ r_br }}px {{ r_bl }}px;
  --expert-quote-radius-mobile: {{ r_tl_m }}px {{ r_tr_m }}px {{ r_br_m }}px {{ r_bl_m }}px;
  --expert-quote-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --expert-quote-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  --expert-quote-gap-x: {{ gap_x }}px;
  --expert-quote-gap-y: {{ gap_y }}px;
  --expert-quote-gap-x-mobile: {{ gap_x_mobile }}px;
  --expert-quote-gap-y-mobile: {{ gap_y_mobile }}px;
  --expert-quote-motion-distance: {{ motion_distance }}px;
  --expert-quote-motion-angle: {{ motion_angle }}deg;
  --expert-quote-motion-scale: {{ motion_scale }};
  --expert-quote-motion-duration: {{ motion_duration }}ms;
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --expert-quote-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --expert-quote-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --expert-quote-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="expert-quote color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1' }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  {%- if s.stack_layer != blank and s.stack_layer != 'default' %} data-section-layer="{{ s.stack_layer }}"{% endif %}
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="expert-quote__inner {% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      `<figure>` rather than a stack of divs: a quotation with the pictures it
      is about is exactly what the element is for, and it lets the quote be a
      real `<blockquote>` and the name a real `<cite>` inside the lead block
      instead of two paragraphs styled to look like an attribution.

      No `<figcaption>`, deliberately. It has to be the figure's first or last
      child to count as one, and the name sits several levels down in the middle
      of the lead — so it would be a `<figcaption>` in name only, announced as a
      caption by nothing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <figure class="expert-quote__figure">
      {% content_for 'block', type: '_expert-quote-lead', id: 'expert-quote-lead' %}

      {%- comment -%}
        The stage. The featured picture is written first so it is read first;
        which side each scattered picture lands on is decided by `order` in
        `assets/base.css` from the block's own Placement setting, and the source
        order the keyboard and the screen reader follow never changes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="{{ stage_classes }}">
        {% content_for 'block', type: '_expert-quote-feature', id: 'expert-quote-feature' %}

        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.expert_quote.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_expert-quote-image"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.expert_quote.paragraphs.blocks"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "container_width",
      "label": "t:shared.container.width.label",
      "info": "t:shared.container.width.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "edge",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "wide",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "standard",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "compact",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__4.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "custom",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__5.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.expert_quote.paragraphs.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "scatter_on_mobile",
      "label": "t:sections.expert_quote.settings.scatter_on_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:sections.expert_quote.settings.scatter_on_mobile.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap_device",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "desktop",
          "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "mobile",
          "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 12,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 12,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.expert_quote.headers.drift"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.expert_quote.paragraphs.drift"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "motion_distance",
      "label": "t:sections.expert_quote.settings.motion_distance.label",
      "info": "t:sections.expert_quote.settings.motion_distance.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 18
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "motion_duration",
      "label": "t:sections.expert_quote.settings.motion_duration.label",
      "info": "t:sections.expert_quote.settings.motion_duration.info",
      "min": 1500,
      "max": 9000,
      "step": 500,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 4000
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:shared.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "background_media",
      "label": "t:shared.background.media.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "image",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "video",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.color.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.color.info",
      "default": "linear-gradient(90deg, #E5F1EE 0%, #FBFDFC 20%, #FBFDFC 40%, #F4F9F8 60%, #EDF5F3 80%, #E5F1EE 100%)",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_position.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "cover",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fit",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "image_parallax",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_parallax.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_parallax.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "image_parallax_speed",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_parallax_speed.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_parallax_speed.info",
      "min": 5,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 15,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' and section.settings.image_parallax }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "video_url",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_url.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video_url.info",
      "accept": [
        "youtube",
        "vimeo"
      ],
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "video_poster",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_poster.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video_poster.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "video_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "cover",
          "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "contain",
          "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_loop",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_loop.label",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "overlay_enabled",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_enabled.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.overlay_enabled.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "overlay_style",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "solid",
          "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "gradient",
          "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_style.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "solid",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media != 'none' and section.settings.overlay_enabled }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "overlay_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_color.label",
      "default": "#000000",
